#---
# purpose: "a guarded recursive clause dispatch never reaches: the static answer says the return is solved, the activation has no recursive call at all"
#---
#
# `step/1`'s first clause wraps its own result in a list, so statically the
# return sits on a productive cycle and every activation of `step/1` owes its
# return to a component solve. The only activation this program has is
# `step/1[:stop]`, which reaches the second clause alone: it makes no call, so
# no call edge joins it to anything. The solve still happens -- a function
# whose return is being solved is a one-member system when nothing else is on
# it -- and the answer is the clause's own `:done`.
def step([value | _]), do: [step(value)]
def step(_), do: :done

def main() do
  dbg(step(:stop))
end
